n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into our expression ${n}^{2}-2n$ and show it is *odd* by writing it as one more than a multiple of $2.$\n\nSubstituting $n=2a+1$ into the expression ${n}^{2}-2n$, we can show that ${n}^{2}-2n=2b+1,$ where $b$ is $\\text{an integer}.$\n\nOnce we've shown this, the proof is complete, and we can state our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, since ${n}^{2}-2n$ $\\text{is one more than}$ a multiple of $2,$ we conclude that ${n}^{2}-2n$ is $\\text{odd}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e3a8b4b8-1277-5bff-9b44-52097a4d5d9a" "answer-field-a0435294-59cb-5278-9c3c-e8274e28bff8" "answer-field-2646ac86-537d-5d63-bd79-59dfde816d03" "answer-field-e1db1f89-1e0f-5cb0-9ef4-729053d6900d" "answer-field-89244946-54e2-53a3-bb36-45af3098ed35" "answer-field-0b3a1b37-5a5a-51bb-be8e-13678a7cce3c" "answer-field-d45c779c-106f-507c-8757-95f98728e006"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e3a8b4b8-1277-5bff-9b44-52097a4d5d9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a8b4b8-1277-5bff-9b44-52097a4d5d9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-d33b0c59-00f7-52e5-9244-5c2dbced2ca2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-34645e00-c069-54cc-b7bc-5f2a7ce4474f" "answer-d33b0c59-00f7-52e5-9244-5c2dbced2ca2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34645e00-c069-54cc-b7bc-5f2a7ce4474f" :answer/id #uuid "34645e00-c069-54cc-b7bc-5f2a7ce4474f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d33b0c59-00f7-52e5-9244-5c2dbced2ca2" :answer/id #uuid "d33b0c59-00f7-52e5-9244-5c2dbced2ca2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a0435294-59cb-5278-9c3c-e8274e28bff8" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0435294-59cb-5278-9c3c-e8274e28bff8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/corr