 even}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is odd.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into the expression $15n+3$ and show it is even by writing it as a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15n+3 & =15(2a+1)+3 \\\\  & =30a+15+3 \\\\  & =30a+18 \\\\  & =2{{(15a+9)}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=15a+9$ (highlighted above), we have that $15n+3=2b,$ which shows that $15n+3$ is indeed a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=15a+9.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15n-3 & =2{{(15a+9)}_{⏟}}_{b} \\\\  & =2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$\n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $15n-3$ is even." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6549ab4-cf9a-5b39-9d10-307c907bf94d" "answer-field-6957b23c-ff11-508d-a5d7-a0c66f7dd5f8" "answer-field-3adeffa5-d35f-5677-a909-c9b47203c1d6" "answer-field-2948be29-96a0-5640-9f15-9a4de7487c71" "answer-field-a960bd7b-2c4e-5988-ae6d-e5e05afe510a" "answer-field-2a663a39-6070-5e22-9cd6-5418e0176583" "answer-field-28a2e34b-b76e-5c88-ad0d-1628dce79163" "answer-field-88c17fc9-8c5c-53f7-8ef6-3002f772d0ac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6549ab4-cf9a-5b39-9d10-307c907bf94d" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6549ab4-cf9a-5b39-9d10-307c907bf94d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-5cfbc41e-74ce-5263-a336-b42e1565ad9b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-29bd0509-84af-516b-8507-8c799b952b2c" "answer-5cfbc41e-74ce-5263-a336-b42e1565ad9b" "answer-15ebd7aa-e160-5337-8622-e5ac4ab0e0d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29bd0509-84af-516b-8507-8c799b952b2c" :answer/id #uuid "29bd0509-84af-516b-8507-8c799b952b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cfbc4