" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-42b2ab24-8440-589b-8253-e7219f00feb7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-42b2ab24-8440-589b-8253-e7219f00feb7" "answer-01a3b71e-fd8a-5eee-b6e8-a1b83053efe5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42b2ab24-8440-589b-8253-e7219f00feb7" :answer/id #uuid "42b2ab24-8440-589b-8253-e7219f00feb7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01a3b71e-fd8a-5eee-b6e8-a1b83053efe5" :answer/id #uuid "01a3b71e-fd8a-5eee-b6e8-a1b83053efe5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157642 :question/problem "Prove that if $n$ is odd, then $3n+5$ is even.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=\\,${{field-1}} for {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & ={{field-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-4}}. Since $a$ is {{field-5}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-6}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n+5$ is {{field-8}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to prove the following:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is odd}\\,⇒\\,3n+5\\text{ is even}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is odd.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into the expression $3n+5$ and show it is even by writing it as a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & =3(2a+1)+5 \\\\  & =6a+3+5 \\\\  & =6a+8 \\\\  & =2{{(3a+4)}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=3a+4$ (highlighted above), we have that $3n+5=2b,$ which shows that $3n+5$ is indeed a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=3a+4.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & =2{{(3a+4)}_{⏟}}_{b} \\\\  & =2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$\n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $3n+5$ is even." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d59b783f-abba-509d-a56c-52c1aa21b3e3" "answer-field-840cd45a-3643-520d-a72d-2dc44a56a38c" "answer-field-8dd8e390-4656-5d19-a030-e4295c43ea4b" "answer-field-56bd3a64-fb7d-52e4-b42a-561d48af6a61" "answer-field-e0a3bf59-d91f-5503-a55b-862d352c357f" "answer-field-1c75a275-3e1c-517e-92eb-6fe31c34f636"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186154162 :answer-field/correct "answer-1ce7407a-d763-527c-b581-7b980b286bc1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ce7407a-d763-527c-b581-7b980b286bc1" "answer-e44bb000-7ee1-5ed0-9042-18c83bd5a075"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ce7407a-d763-527c-b581-7b980b286bc1" :answer/id #uuid "1ce7407a-d763-527c-b581-7b980b286bc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2a+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e44bb000-7ee1-5ed0-9042-18c83bd5a075" :answer/id #uuid "e44bb000-7ee1-5ed0-9042-18c83bd5a075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{a+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186154158 :answer-field/correct 17592186154159 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d59b783f-abba-509d-a56c-52c1aa21b3e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d59b783f-abba-509d-a56c-52c1aa21b3e3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f7d1575c-fc51-515d-b257-04a83857a6ea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1c83e34-c9ab-541b-a2c7-b1fd6d22a5c0" "answer-a3ae77ff-e334-537b-b623-2ff5c9eedc89" "answer-bb62b3ea-ae3d-509a-bef5-c2cbde5718be" "answer-dd673df8-8be3-57bb-b5df-665045362758" "answer-f7d1575c-fc51-515d-b257-04a83857a6ea" "answer-da8e89b1-2538-5d5c-b7f1-c1dff7506fcb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answe