ld/correct "answer-2a866151-9906-5219-93ae-9093dafbea30" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a866151-9906-5219-93ae-9093dafbea30" "answer-75a1030c-0678-5696-96c3-cfd28e7ffdf2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a866151-9906-5219-93ae-9093dafbea30" :answer/id #uuid "2a866151-9906-5219-93ae-9093dafbea30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75a1030c-0678-5696-96c3-cfd28e7ffdf2" :answer/id #uuid "75a1030c-0678-5696-96c3-cfd28e7ffdf2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2a01950-32bd-52d0-9e4d-1134c0e8e132" :question/id #uuid "b2a01950-32bd-52d0-9e4d-1134c0e8e132" :question/math-academy-id "q-184289" :question/problem "Prove that if $n$ is an odd integer, then $7n+4$ is odd.\n\nLet $n$ be an odd integer. Then, $n=\\,${{field-1}} for some integer $a.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7n+4 & ={{field-2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-3}}. Since $a$ is {{field-4}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-5}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7n+4 & ={{field-6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is one larger than a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $7n+4$ is {{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to show the following:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is odd}\\,⇒\\,7n+4\\text{ is odd}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is odd.\n\nLet $n$ be an odd integer. Then, $n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into our expression $7n+4$ and show it is odd by writing it as a multiple of $2,$ plus $1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7n+4 & =7(2a+1)+4 \\\\  & =14a+7+4 \\\\  & =(14a+10)+1 \\\\  & =2{{(7a+5)}_{⏟}}_{b}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=7a+5$ (highlighted above), we have that $7n+4=2b+1,$ which shows that $7n+4$ is indeed one more than a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=7a+5.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7n+4 & =2{{(7a+5)}_{⏟}}_{b}+1 \\\\  & =2b+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is one larger than a multiple of $2.$ \n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $7n+4$ is odd." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7710be6a-f583-50cc-be1e-887148befb2f" "answer-field-88aefc3b-85b7-5ebf-86b5-3b311a392b3a" "answer-field-b7c7c58e-2566-575d-854c-b821b813649e" "answer-field-c3ec463e-4414-530a-9f98-5ebd6c06b1d9" "answer-field-9f5c494c-00ec-5406-9244-eb92baf01861" "answer-field-0a6b19e0-11fb-59c0-87e4-13aac54b6540" "answer-field-bf251810-fc22-5932-932b-54a908c024c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7710be6a-f583-50cc-be1e-887148befb2f" :answer-field/id #uuid "7710be6a-f583-50cc-be1e-887148befb2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ffbedf2a-0de5-5b6d-9607-adc4f1bca01c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2938a77f-638a-598a-920d-939781b66aa4" "answer-ffbedf2a-0de5-5b6d-9607-adc4f1bca01c" "answer-cbc6bb23-f9bd-5007-ad5c-9fe359c416cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2938a77f-638a-598a-920d-939781b66aa4" :answer/id #uuid "2938a77f-638a-598a-920d-939781b66aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffbedf2a-0de5-5b6d-9607-adc4f1bca01c" :answer/id #uuid "ffbedf2a-0de5-5b6d-9607-adc4f1bca01c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2a+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbc6bb23-f9bd-5007-ad5c-9fe359c416cf" :answer/id #uuid "cbc6bb23-f9bd-5007-ad5c-9fe359c416cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{a+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-88aefc3b-85b7-5ebf-86b5-3b311a392b3a" :answer-field/id #uuid "88aefc3b-85b