c3f142-3aca-55ec-9553-fc80a22aeca2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2b+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d98842d0-3beb-540b-8a83-82146fd2a3c7" :answer/id #uuid "d98842d0-3beb-540b-8a83-82146fd2a3c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2b-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bf251810-fc22-5932-932b-54a908c024c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf251810-fc22-5932-932b-54a908c024c8" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-41a95b4c-51e4-5805-b964-452a39e3faca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f2960c28-b6ce-5287-9382-2bf576f6e4ec" "answer-41a95b4c-51e4-5805-b964-452a39e3faca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2960c28-b6ce-5287-9382-2bf576f6e4ec" :answer/id #uuid "f2960c28-b6ce-5287-9382-2bf576f6e4ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41a95b4c-51e4-5805-b964-452a39e3faca" :answer/id #uuid "41a95b4c-51e4-5805-b964-452a39e3faca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-777be974-f06f-56a1-8838-5bb4b1e9b194" :question/id #uuid "777be974-f06f-56a1-8838-5bb4b1e9b194" :question/math-academy-id "q-184291" :question/problem "Prove that  $9n-8$ is odd if $n$ is an odd integer.\n\nLet $n$ be an odd integer. Then, $n=\\,${{field-1}} for some integer $a.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & ={{field-2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-3}}. Since $a$ is {{field-4}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-5}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & ={{field-6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is one larger than a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $9n-8$ is {{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to show the following:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is odd}\\,⇒\\,9n-8\\text{ is odd}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is odd.\n\nLet $n$ be an odd integer. Then, $n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into our expression $9n-8$ and show it is odd by writing it as a multiple of $2,$ plus $1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & =9(2a+1)-8 \\\\  & =18a+9-8 \\\\  & =2{{(9a)}_{⏟}}_{b}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=9a$ (highlighted above), we have that $9n-8=2b+1,$ which shows that $9n-8$ is indeed one more than a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=9a.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & =2{{(9a)}_{⏟}}_{b}+1 \\\\  & =2b+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is one larger than a multiple of $2.$ \n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $9n-8$ is odd." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6576973c-5c23-50d0-af5c-c294655aeb63" "answer-field-0a120ac5-8ff4-5dc2-80b2-e8dc2915a38f" "answer-field-fc0855dd-1d56-55a1-9092-50acbc482061" "answer-field-3931611b-dc53-5b7a-9a30-18ab07e988e2" "answer-field-79df9a1b-c57c-517d-b519-c412739f1c20" "answer-field-64d112f4-10c5-57c8-8749-e47c2dee5045" "answer-field-984e6594-129d-5f16-ac1e-883b51e34aea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6576973c-5c23-50d0-af5c-c294655aeb63" :answer-field/id #uuid "6576973c-5c23-50d0-af5c-c294655aeb63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-87b0b01f-40a6-5cc1-ba39-397359460303" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b74adccc-1216-5c19-acb4-29a820187629" "answer-87b0b01f-40a6-5cc1-ba39-397359460303" "answer-985a156b-84c9-504b-bd36-6584878f8979"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b74adccc-1216-5c19-acb4-29a820187629" :answer/id #uuid "b74adccc-1216-5c19-acb4-29a820187629" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {: